  "notes": "The 2011–2015 ATL minimal-melodic bench: one hooky two-bar synth cell and nothing under it. The research's own words for the method are \"volume-and-space rather than layering\", so the identifying numbers here are subtractive — `melody.densityPerBar` [2,5] for a 3–6 pitch motif, `contour.riff` 0.72 because the cell repeats rather than develops, no pad layer expressed as a heavily `vamp`-weighted harmonic rhythm and `impliedByRiff`, and `octaveJumpProb` down at 0.12 where the club-facing bench beside it sits at 0.3. What is *not* subtractive is the 808: the research says it is loud relative to the melody with 16th repeats, so it keeps the genre's medium distortion and gets `glideProb` 0.35 for the short glides. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates it high-medium and says explicitly that the tempo figures are generalized — `session.bpm` is the inferred parameter here, read off a career-level range rather than off records. ⚠ The i–VI and i–VII families are what the research names as \"two-chord beds\"; the static `i` on top of them is the \"single riff over a static tonic\" case. Chord variety is carried by `chordDurationBeats` and three harmonic rhythms, not by progressions this producer does not play.",
